    <!-- ─── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="nfaq" id="faq">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="nfaq__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">FAQ · Notes</span>
          <h2>The four things people ask first.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            If your question is not here, the
            <a href="/faq.html">full FAQ</a> covers privacy, performance, and
            comparison.
          </p>
        </header>
        <ul class="nfaq__list" role="list">
          <li>
            <details class="nfaq__item" id="q-vs-evernote-notion-obsidian">
              <summary class="nfaq__q">
                <span class="nfaq__q-text">Is this Evernote? Notion? Obsidian?</span>
                <span class="nfaq__caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="nfaq__body">
                <p class="nfaq__a">
                  Local-first like Obsidian. Voice-first like nothing else.
                  Free forever like Evernote once was, before it stopped being.
                  The data model is plain SQLite plus a markdown body, so it
                  opens in any tool you already use.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="nfaq__item" id="q-read-messages">
              <summary class="nfaq__q">
                <span class="nfaq__q-text">Does Pulse read my messages?</span>
                <span class="nfaq__caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="nfaq__body">
                <p class="nfaq__a">
                  Only what you choose to share. There is no SMS access, no
                  notification listener, no accessibility-service trick that
                  quietly scans other apps. The capture sheet opens only when
                  you tap "share to Pulse" in another app. That's the entire
                  surface.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="nfaq__item" id="q-sync-between-devices">
              <summary class="nfaq__q">
                <span class="nfaq__q-text">Can I sync notes between phone and desktop?</span>
                <span class="nfaq__caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="nfaq__body">
                <p class="nfaq__a">
                  In the v0.5 release, Pulse is single-device. The Pro tier
                  (planned, $5/mo) will add opt-in end-to-end-encrypted sync
                  across your devices. If you want it now, the
                  <code>notes.db</code> file is a plain SQLite database —
                  point any git client at <code>~/.pulse</code> and you have
                  free, manual sync.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="nfaq__item" id="q-leave-pulse">
              <summary class="nfaq__q">
                <span class="nfaq__q-text">What if I want to leave?</span>
                <span class="nfaq__caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="nfaq__body">
                <p class="nfaq__a">
                  Your <code>notes.db</code> is plain SQLite. Open it with any
                  database browser (DB Browser for SQLite, sqlite3 CLI,
                  Beekeeper Studio) and your data is right there. Export to
                  markdown from Settings → Data, one click, one .zip. No
                  export cap, no "premium-only" feature, no retention.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

